## Thresholds h, δ and τ

h(n_c) and δ(N) come from S0-vs-S0 calibration runs ({{t009.thresholds.settings.cases_per_cell}} incidents per cell, repeats {{t009.thresholds.settings.repeats}}); τ_cell is the oracle threshold per cell.

| Metric | h({{design.t009b.h_n}}) | False rejection of h | δ({{design.t009b.delta_n}}) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| CD | {{t009b.h.cd.70.h}} | {{t009b.h.cd.70.achieved_false_rejection}} | {{t009b.delta.cd.420}} |
| ES | {{t009b.h.es.70.h}} | {{t009b.h.es.70.achieved_false_rejection}} | {{t009b.delta.es.420}} |

τ_cell on CD by cell: bad_deployment/L1 {{t009b.tau.cd.bad_deployment/L1}}, bad_deployment/L2 {{t009b.tau.cd.bad_deployment/L2}}, dependency_failure/L1 {{t009b.tau.cd.dependency_failure/L1}}, dependency_failure/L2 {{t009b.tau.cd.dependency_failure/L2}}, traffic_spike/L1 {{t009b.tau.cd.traffic_spike/L1}}, traffic_spike/L2 {{t009b.tau.cd.traffic_spike/L2}}.

