Fitness of the oracle (pre-registered F) asks whether some control moves the L1 and L2 cells of one family apart, by opposite signs beyond τ or by a large size gap, so that per-cell scoring can matter. CD: {{t009b.fitness.cd.fit}} (sign rule met: {{t009b.fitness.cd.sign_met}}, size rule met: {{t009b.fitness.cd.size_met}}); ES: {{t009b.fitness.es.fit}} (sign rule met: {{t009b.fitness.es.sign_met}}, size rule met: {{t009b.fitness.es.size_met}}).

## Null label rates (planning estimate)

For a candidate with no effect, the planning simulation gave a Local Harm label rate of {{t009b.null_label_rate_plan.local_harm}} and a Severe Local Harm rate of {{t009b.null_label_rate_plan.severe}}. Because τ_cell equals ε, Local Harm is broad; Severe is the primary label.
